// genra clip writer: toolkit poses -> hybrid Humanoid clip on the package's catalog prefab, measured in Unity.
// Rendered by tools/genra/unity_clip.py ({{JOB}} {{OUTPUT}}) and run with the gateway's eval_file in Edit Mode.
// Mapped Humanoid bones become muscle and body (RootT/RootQ) curves from HumanPoseHandler; every other joint keeps
// exact local transform curves. Root motion is baked into the pose: PlayerRenderer plays clips through Animancer
// with applyRootMotion off, so nothing may be extracted from the body. Playback is measured the same way in a
// preview scene. The clip is saved only when the job names a new asset path; nothing is overwritten or bound.
var job = Newtonsoft.Json.Linq.JObject.Parse(System.IO.File.ReadAllText("{{JOB}}"));
var output = "{{OUTPUT}}";
